$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: usm/gen-user-docs
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-26"
summary: >-
  Personas and journey flows (actor/surface per step) become first-class spec data; a new user-doc
  generator composes task-oriented user guides and Playwright e2e skeletons from persona journeys;
  help docs for feature pages are composed from persona/journey content instead of filtering
  developer docs. Backward compatible: flows without persona actors stay pipeline flows in the
  developer stream. Schema shipped: personas[] on system.usm, actor/surface on flows/steps;
  tests[].flow already existed. Dogfooding note resolved: this spec's own flows are annotated with
  actor/surface.
$system: usm/system
$service: usm/cli
intent: >-
  Restores the founding vision: the spec holds personas, UI journeys, and e2e-testable flows, so
  user documentation is COMPOSED from that data (persona guides, task-oriented walkthroughs) while
  developer docs remain a separate stream. Today's help docs are produced by subtracting developer
  content from developer docs — the reverse of the vision — and the schema cannot express personas
  or UI interactions at all. This feature makes personas and journey flows first-class, generates
  user docs from them, derives Playwright e2e skeletons from the same journeys, and replaces
  subtraction-based help docs for feature pages with composition.
status: built
flows:
  - id: author-personas-journeys
    name: Author personas and journey flows
    steps:
      - action: add
        actor: spec-author
        id: s1
        surface: spec
        target: personas[] to system.usm (id, name, description)
      - action: annotate
        actor: spec-author
        id: s2
        surface: spec
        target: flows with actor (flow-level or per-step) and optional surface, marking them as journeys
      - action: validate
        actor: agent
        id: s3
        target: >-
          schema: persona ids referenced by actor exist; unknown actors rejected (hard error in
          generate pass)
      - action: review
        actor: spec-author
        id: s4
        surface: browser
        target: composed user docs rendered live via usm docs serve
  - id: generate-user-docs
    name: Generate user documentation from personas and journeys
    steps:
      - action: parses
        actor: agent
        id: s1
        target: personas from system.usm, journey flows across all feature specs
      - action: composes
        actor: agent
        id: s2
        target: per-persona guide sections; each journey becomes a task-oriented guide page
      - action: renders
        actor: agent
        id: s3
        target: persona steps as instructions, system/agent steps as 'the system will …' statements
      - action: writes
        actor: agent
        id: s4
        target: user-docs output tree; developer stream untouched
  - id: generate-e2e-specs
    name: Generate e2e specs from journeys
    steps:
      - action: selects
        actor: agent
        id: s1
        target: journey flows with linked tests[] entries (tests[].flow reference)
      - action: emits
        actor: agent
        id: s2
        target: Playwright .spec.ts skeletons per journey under tests/auto-generated/e2e/
      - action: preserves
        actor: agent
        id: s3
        target: existing Vitest generation for non-journey tests
  - id: help-docs-composed
    name: Compose help docs from user content
    steps:
      - action: composes
        actor: agent
        id: s1
        target: feature pages in help docs from summary, intent, and journey guides
      - action: retains
        actor: agent
        id: s2
        target: subtraction filter for non-feature (system-level) help pages only
      - action: deprecates
        actor: agent
        id: s3
        target: subtraction path for feature pages, kept functional for one transition cycle
contracts:
  - id: personas-first-class
    description: >-
      system.usm gains personas[] — id, name, description. Flows and steps gain optional actor
      (persona id, or 'system'/'agent') and optional surface (e.g. ui, cli, api).
    must_have:
      - "personas[] validates: unique ids, non-empty name"
      - actor values either reference a declared persona id or are system/agent
      - validate fails on unknown persona references (typo protection)
      - existing specs without personas/actor validate unchanged
  - id: journeys-vs-pipelines
    description: >-
      A flow is a journey when its actor (flow-level or step-level) references a persona; otherwise
      it is a pipeline and behaves exactly as today.
    must_have:
      - flows with default (no) actor default to system and stay in the developer stream
      - journeys render in user docs; pipelines never do
      - step-level actor overrides flow-level default
  - id: user-docs-composed
    description: >-
      New user-doc generator composes guides from personas and journeys — never by filtering
      developer content.
    must_have:
      - "one guide page per journey: task-oriented title from flow name, ordered steps"
      - >-
        steps with actor=system/agent rendered as 'the system …' prose, persona steps as
        instructions
      - per-persona navigation grouping (Guides for <persona>)
      - generation is idempotent and deterministic
  - id: e2e-from-journeys
    description: >-
      tests[] gains optional flow reference; journey tests emit Playwright e2e skeletons alongside
      existing Vitest output.
    must_have:
      - >-
        tests with flow referencing a journey emit a valid Playwright .spec.ts under
        tests/auto-generated/e2e/
      - "output path derives from exact feature $id — collision-free (issue #37 class)"
      - tests without flow ref continue to generate Vitest specs unchanged
  - id: help-composition-replaces-subtraction
    description: >-
      Feature pages in help docs are composed from summary, intent, and public journey guides; the
      subtraction filter is deprecated but stays functional for system-level pages.
    must_have:
      - help feature pages contain no contracts/tests/implementation sections
      - help feature pages embed the journey guides relevant to public personas
      - existing --audience help still runs and produces a valid site (non-feature pages unchanged)
      - no user-visible regression for projects with no personas defined
  - id: backward-compatible
    description: >-
      Projects that never declare personas get byte-identical generated output to the previous
      version.
    must_have:
      - all existing generators unchanged when no personas/journey actors present
      - schema changes are additive and optional-only
      - existing .usm files validate with no edits required
tests:
  - expect:
      - assertion: usm validate rejects unknown persona reference in flow actor
      - assertion: usm validate accepts persona id, system, and agent actors
    id: persona-validation
    setup:
      spec_with_flow_actor_referencing_undeclared_persona: true
  - expect:
      - assertion: user-docs guide page exists with flow name as task title
      - assertion: persona steps rendered as instructions, system steps as system statements
      - assertion: developer feature page unchanged in shape and content
    id: journey-renders-guide
    setup:
      feature_with_persona_actor_flow: true
  - expect:
      - assertion: no user-docs output for that flow
      - assertion: developer doc and Vitest generation identical to pre-change output
    id: pipeline-flows-unchanged
    setup:
      feature_with_flows_without_actor: true
  - expect:
      - assertion: Playwright .spec.ts generated under tests/auto-generated/e2e/ with valid syntax
      - assertion: >-
          no output path collision between two features defining the same journey id (exact $id
          parsing, issue #37 class)
      - assertion: tests without flow reference still produce Vitest specs only
    id: e2e-specs-from-journeys
    setup:
      journey_with_linked_tests: true
  - expect:
      - assertion: help feature page contains journey guide content and no contracts/tests sections
      - assertion: help docs build succeeds for a project with zero personas (regression guard)
    id: help-page-composition
    setup:
      public_feature_with_journeys: true
  - expect:
      - assertion: second run produces byte-identical output
      - assertion: no orphan files from removed flows
    id: idempotent-generation
    setup:
      generate_run_twice: true
decisions:
  - decision: Implement the full composition model in one feature — no phased rollout
    id: single-vision-not-staged
    rationale: >-
      Staged approaches lose intent — the human explicitly rejected phases. Contracts encode the end
      state (composition replaces subtraction for feature pages), so partial implementations fail
      review instead of shipping half a vision. Roadmap entries are written in the same session as
      the spec, not deferred.
    status: accepted
  - decision: "Personas stay minimal: id, name, description — no goals/frustrations/expertise yet"
    id: minimal-personas
    rationale: >-
      Starts authoring via MCP tools without schema bloat; the composition generator only needs
      identity and context today. Fields can be added additively later without migration.
    status: accepted
  - decision: >-
      Step actor defaults to system; flows without a persona actor remain pipeline flows in
      developer docs
    id: actor-default-system
    rationale: >-
      Current flows (parse→generate→write) are genuinely pipeline steps. Making actor optional
      preserves them untouched and keeps backward compatibility byte-exact.
    status: accepted
  - decision: E2E linkage via optional tests[].flow reference — not steps referencing tests
    id: e2e-link-via-tests
    rationale: >-
      Assertions already live in tests[]; a flow reference ties them to journeys without duplicating
      steps in two places. The journey provides the narrative, the linked tests provide the
      assertions, one source each.
    status: accepted
  - decision: Deprecate (do not delete) the --audience help subtraction filter for feature pages
    id: filter-deprecated-not-deleted
    rationale: >-
      System-level pages (getting started, references) still need filtering; feature pages switch to
      composition. Keeping the filter functional avoids breaking consumers while the composed path
      becomes the default for features.
    status: accepted
implementation:
  primary: src/generators/userDocs.ts
  test_code: tests/userDocs.test.ts
  test_code_status: manual
see_also:
  - usm/gen-docs-split
  - usm/gen-testspecs
  - usm/gen-feature-review
  - usm/gen-roadmap
